  "worked_solution": "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 41\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 41\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 41\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -13 & 26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -13{x}_{2}=26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(-2)=-3\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-9)+(-2)=-11.$",
